# Inc-R2 RED proofs + verification transcript — Lane R, batch 2026-10-10-perf-batch

Worker: Kimi (kimi-code/kimi-for-coding) via the kimi CLI. All commands run from
the worktree root; all paths relative. Product change under test: the unscaled
`_tree_layout` memo in `mapper/views/layered.py` (instance storage on
`LayeredRenderer`, strong-reference key, `_layout_misses` spy) +
`tests/test_perf_layout_memo.py`. Bytecode cache off (`python -B`,
`-p no:cacheprovider`).

## 0 · The product change (GREEN state)

`mapper/views/layered.py`: `_tree_layout_unscaled` (slot + level per node) is
memoised on the owning `LayeredRenderer` instance and passed into module-level
`_geometry` as an argument (no module-global state, ruling R12). The key is
strong references compared with `is` plus lengths (`graph`, its `edges` list
(+len), its `nodes` dict (+len), `root_id`, `hidden`); a hit re-applies the
`card_w`/`gap` scaling per call. Misses are counted on the instance spy
`_layout_misses` at the hit check.

sha256 of the shipped `mapper/views/layered.py` (before any mutation, and
restored to, byte-identically, after every mutation):

    3e34fd90426b30fc9dbdf4dc8ade90de8ba7404ab232c58283c124d6e8e04743 *mapper/views/layered.py

Restore command used after every mutation:

    $ cp .dev-flow/2026-10-10-perf-batch/evidence/r2-layered-memo.py mapper/views/layered.py
    $ sha256sum mapper/views/layered.py
    3e34fd90426b30fc9dbdf4dc8ade90de8ba7404ab232c58283c124d6e8e04743 *mapper/views/layered.py

## 1 · Measured layout computations, AT-075 session (before vs after)

BEFORE (pre-Inc-R2 `layered.py` at HEAD, same wide-2000 nav session):
`evidence/perf0c-nav.transcript:44` —

    _tree_layout  mapper\views\layered.py:192   ncalls=10  (2 renders)

i.e. ~5 `_tree_layout` computations per render, none cached.

AFTER (shipped memo, AT-075b six-key session at 118x34 through the real app,
from the GREEN run in §2 with `-s`):

    AT-075b memo misses after open + l,j,j,j,j: 1
    AT-075b memo misses after archive + l: 2

One unscaled layout computation now covers open + five selection-only
keypresses (six paints); the archive (a structural edit) costs exactly one more.
Selection-only navigation went from ~5 layout computations per render to zero.

